			<div class="content" id="post-content-3893559">
									

<p>This is incredible for a first contribution. I loved it. I'm happy to be one of the first to upvote it.</p>
<p>The only thing which really bugs me is the expungement at the end. I'm not sure what you had in mind (ideally, you should have an idea of what you are expunging, rather than just doing it for looks) but it seems like it might be important information. By taking it out, not only are you implying something has happened to Site-41, but more importantly are making the overt statement that the mere thought Lecroy is correct is vastly important, regardless of the actual nature of the previous iteration of Site-41. I'm not sure that statement alone is convincing. The expungement in 4000-B is a bit more forgivable, since is more subtle.</p>
<p>But still, +1. This kept my attention since I started reading it.</p>
<p>Also, with a title like &quot;It Won't Stop Screaming&quot; I expected some cliche article with a rating of -14 written by a 12-year-old kid who wanted to write a crazy screaming monster. I'm glad this wasn't the case; you really took the time to write a good article.</p>

							</div>

								
