														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3894261">
									

<p>This was pretty darn good, though I'll admit to being somewhat put out by the ending. There's all this buildup, but no real indication of what's being hinted at.</p>
<p>I have one big suggestion for you: be more up-front about the &quot;buried for four million years&quot; thing in the description. You front-load the description with all the stuff that can't affect this guy, and it comes off like a bog-standard X-man skip that way. The age and his condition are far more interesting; start with that, then mention he's impervious to injury and doesn't age, then tell us he looks exactly like a current Foundation researcher. I recommend leaving that part for last because it's a good segue into the meat of the story here, and it just suggests so much.</p>

							</div>

								
					
