														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3894283">
									

<p>Thanks for the feedback TL333s.</p>
<p>I've given a fuller outline of the ending and my reasons for writing it the way that I did in my reply to Werdna. Can I ask which bit you found particularly problematic? I'm considering changing some elements.</p>
<p>It's a good thought, and honestly I'd have liked to write it that way. Really, the idea came to me from the moment of discovery, so the first two sections are built backwards from that. But the SCP style seems to me to make it difficult to change things around too much.</p>
<p>I'm not sure how I would talk about the burial if I hadn't already explained why it was possible. If the first thing you read was that he'd been stuck underground, it might feel a bit out of place. Plus, having the 'can't lose consciousness' thing after it rather than before it takes away a bit of the horror of the situation. And SCPs generally begin with a physical description rather than situation or powers. As I have it now, the physical description of scars leads into the physical invulnerability, which leads to lack of losing hair, which leads to lack of ageing.</p>
<p>If I could think of a way of writing it in your order without making it feel too non-clinical, I would, but I'm not sure how I'd go about it right now.</p>

							</div>

								
					
