				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/uncannyon" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4374851); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4374851&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608238168" alt="Uncannyon" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4374851)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/uncannyon" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4374851); return false;" >Uncannyon</a></span> <span class="odate time_1533257983 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">03 Aug 2018 00:59</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3896166">
									

<p><strong>Update – 02.08.2018</strong></p>
<p>Thanks to everyone who's provided their thoughts and comments since the original posting.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Explanation</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Explanation</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>So, due to pretty consistent feedback I’ve spent the last couple of hours tinkering with Addendum 2. I’ve come up with a version which I think improves on the original in several areas, but ultimately I’ve reached a slightly more radical conclusion.</p>
<p>I think it might be to the benefit of the SCP to simply remove Addendum 2 altogether. Even my revised version doesn’t really do what people seem to want of it. The last section of an SCP is often the ‘punch’ and while Addendum 2 was not intended to be this, having it as the ending seems to be diffusing the intrigue generated by the main article rather than acting as the ‘I want to learn more’ cliff-hanger I intended it to be.</p>
<p>Moreover, Addendum 2 does not initially appear to be particularly relevant to the majority of this SCP. While it is set up by an earlier section of the document, it doesn’t really elaborate on anything further and instead just creates more questions. Which can absolutely work – creating frustrating unanswered questions is still a major theme of this SCP – but given that Addendum 1 also does this, having it again in Addendum 2, and with far less context, is perhaps not a very effective feature.</p>
<p>In creating Addendum 2, I think I was working by what I considered interesting in the overall narrative I’m trying to create rather than focusing on what is important to this specific piece of writing.</p>
<p>So, I’m removing Addendum 2 for now. I do still have both the original and the updated version if people feel this isn’t a change for the better, or that some part of Addendum 2 is worth salvaging. <strong>Opinions on the matter are very welcome.</strong></p>
<p>In order not to completely lose my Site-41 breadcrumb dropping, I’m making a small addition to Addendum 1 in its place. A full log of changes is below.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Changes</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Changes</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ul>
<li>Addendum 2 has been removed.</li>
<li>An additional reference to Site-41 has been added to SCP-4000-B</li>
<li>A comment on this reference, and an already existing one, has been added to Carter’s second report, essentially conveying what would have replaced the final redacted line in the previous version.</li>
<li>The [DATA EXPUNGED] used to conceal the identity of the individual prohibiting a line of investigation has been changed to O5-██ to give a slightly bigger hint at what is not being investigated.</li>
<li>The line “I hardly need to spell out the importance of the information it could potentially provide to the Foundation” has been removed for being clichéd and a bit trite.</li>
<li>Half a dozen sentences have received minor tweaks to make them scan a little better.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>As always, feedback is welcome and appreciated.</strong></p>

