<blockquote>
<p>This was pretty darn good, though I'll admit to being somewhat put out by the ending. There's all this buildup, but no real indication of what's being hinted at.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This comment was from a previous version, but I found myself agreeing. A ton of buildup, and no payoff. The concept is cliche, on many levels, to be honest. I <em>like</em> the concept, though, and the stylistic execution almost saves it, but too many cliche elements are kept: Generic Standard Male Everyday Foundation Researcher, generic spooky sentiments avoiding any specific future clarifications, an odd aversion to experimentation that might actually clarify some things, not-quite-believable reaction to being sealed away so long &#8212; why screaming? why not simple catatonia? &#8212; etc.</p>
<p>Even if all those were changed, this feels like it's missing most of a story, and it lacks payoff.</p>
<p>Out of curiosity, I looked at the old addendum. That wouldn't have been enough payoff for me either, FWIW. It's just there.</p>

